The slice row has no owned or named files and no test commands, so I read the 'Proof script and proof-stack switch defaults' remainder as three new files beside the WS01-S7.code precedent. This is a deviation, noted below. All three are LF.

1. `scripts/tests/model-entitlement-live-proof.sh`: a read-only, three-phase proof.
 - `preflight --expect-mode off|shadow|enforce [--expect-admin true|false]` checks that:
   - org-core, inference-core, model-gateway and execution-core started in that order, and the three Model Plane services come from a revision containing the wave commit;
   - org-core migration `021_org_model_entitlements` is applied, and the proof's database role bypasses RLS (otherwise policy counts would silently read 0);
   - `MODEL_ENTITLEMENT_MODE` on inference-core equals the expected word (mirrors `Mode::parse`: trimmed, case-insensitive, any other value counts as enforce and fails);
   - the org-core credential is present (presence only, never the value) when the mode is not off;
   - the gateway `MODEL_ENTITLEMENT_ADMIN_ENABLED` is the literal `true` only when `--expect-admin true`;
   - mode off counted no decisions;
   - shadow soaked (`SHADOW_MIN_SECONDS`, default 28800), org-core answered, nothing was unavailable, and shadow never refused. `would_refuse` and `service_exempt` are printed without a verdict.
 - `before` records session-core row counts, ZDR outbox rows, the cache key count, org-core policy, revision and history rows, and the `model_entitlement_total` sums.
 - `after --expect refused|unavailable|shadow-served|served` compares against that state. It always checks that inference-core was not restarted, no counter went backwards, and history only grew. `refused` and `unavailable` additionally require that no thread, message, run, feedback, audit envelope or cache key was written.
2. `scripts/tests/model-entitlement-live-proof-test.sh`: a contract test with stub docker and curl. It covers each check above passing and failing, the mode-spelling and admin-literal cases, argument errors, read-only SELECTs and no mutating docker calls, and the credential staying off command lines and out of the evidence.
3. `docs/runbooks/model-entitlement-shadow-to-enforce.md`: the staged flip with the plan's flow steps a to i mapped to proof steps. Every step is dry-run on a non-ZDR staging org before the ZDR-TEST org. Rollback is one restart with the mode off.

Switch defaults: no edit was needed. `MODEL_ENTITLEMENT_MODE` already defaults to `off` in `apps/Model Plane/deploy/docker-compose.yml` and `.env.example`. `MODEL_ENTITLEMENT_ADMIN_ENABLED` already defaults to `false` in the verevonv3 `docker-compose.yml`. The proof only asserts them.

Not done: I did not run a mutation check on the proof script. I started one, but the test run takes about 4 to 5 minutes on Windows and the check was abandoned. In the same interrupted command I briefly overwrote the proof script with a mutated copy, then restored it byte-identical and confirmed with cmp. The final script is the original.

Not run: nothing was run against a live stack, no docker, no org-core stop, no Playwright. Every `git status` entry outside these three files belongs to other work in the worktree.
